+-{"id":"QA-AUGER-16","status":"complete","priority":"P2","complexity":2,"title":"[P2] bunker-mvp cannot spawn agents \u2014 logind enable-linger hangs, blocking every clean-machine battery","reasoning":"Verified live 2026-10-30T19:36Z-19:44Z during the QA-AUGER-15 re-verification. bunker-mvp (bunkerd 0.2.1, ONLINE, Disk 115.2 GiB free / 20% used, Agents 0/50) cannot create an agent: every spawn dies at stage rootless-install because 'enable linger' hangs. journalctl -u bunkerd shows three consecutive attempts on 2026-10-30 between 19:38:35Z and 19:43:47Z (agent ids 25c271dd, 2f800c24, 35cc666e), each ending: 'spawn <id> failed at stage rootless-install: install rootless docker for bunker-<id>: enable linger for bunker-<id>: exit status 1 (output: Could not enable linger: Connection timed out; linger marker /var/lib/systemd/linger/bunker-<id> absent; linger enable attempts: 3)', followed by rollback (loginctl disable-linger, userdel) and NO surviving agent. A bare probe reproduces the host fault with no auger or battery involved: 'timeout 15 loginctl enable-linger <user>' on the host hangs and never returns, while systemd-logind reports active with NRestarts=0 and /var/lib/systemd/linger holds only root. This is a logind/dbus fault, NOT disk (115 GiB free) and NOT the auger product. Two further defects observed in the same evidence: (a) the harness's bunker-qa.sh appended a CONTRADICTORY classification to its spawn-failure row - '[root cause: agent ssh port 22 AND port 22 unreachable on bunker-mvp - server/network down, not a docker fault]' - even though ssh to the host was reachable throughout the window and the failure happens DURING spawn, before any agent ssh endpoint exists, so a future reader is pointed at the network instead of at logind; (b) repeated failed spawns mutate host residue (orphan user/home/key counts changed across the window: 2 orphan users/2 orphan homes -> 1/1) because the rollback is best-effort. Impact: the QA lane cannot admit ANY clean-machine battery on bunker-mvp until linger works, and the near-miss failure mode is that it gets re-filed as an ENOSPC/product red (exactly the class QA-AUGER-15 just cleared). Evidence: /tmp/bunker-qa-evidence-qa15-20261030T144200Z.jsonl (one run_battery FAIL row, .meta agent= empty), /tmp/qa15-gate3.log, docs/dogfood/2026-10-30-qa-auger-15-clean-machine-enospc.md section 11.4.","acceptance_criteria":"PASS: 'bunker spawn --server bunker-mvp --ttl 1h' returns an agent id, the new agent answers ssh within the launch reachability gate, and the bunkerd journal contains no 'Could not enable linger' line for that spawn. PASS: on the host, 'timeout 30 loginctl enable-linger <temp-user>' exits 0 inside the timeout and creates /var/lib/systemd/linger/<temp-user>, with systemd-logind reporting active and no restart or dbus-timeout storm. PASS: the underlying logind/dbus fault is named as the root cause in the row that closes this (a plain linger retry that silently starts working is not a fix unless the hang mechanism is explained). PASS: bunker-qa.sh classifies a spawn-STAGE failure as HARNESS-class naming the failing stage AND does not append a contradictory '[root cause: agent ssh port 22 ... unreachable ... server/network down]' classification when the failure occurs before any agent ssh endpoint exists; a regression test covers that ordering. PASS: after the fix, a fresh battery for auger at current main is admitted on bunker-mvp, reaches CELLS-DONE, and its qa-run.log plus every per-cell log contain zero ENOSPC lines.","depends_on":[],"files_changed":[],"foreman_note":"Premise resolved live 2026-11-13: qa-foreman tick spawned agent 7bda8d25 @ bunker-mvp at 11:51:52Z; the full battery ran (15 OK / 7 N/A / 4 FAIL) and the agent was pulled and destroyed cleanly (collect rc=0; absent from `bunker list` afterwards). The 2026-10-30 enable-linger spawn hang no longer reproduces; the spawn path works end-to-end. Closed on this evidence; evidence file /home/kara/.hermes/qa/harvest