++ {"id":"AUG-122","status":"complete","priority":"P1","complexity":4,"title":"[P1] Resolve a task or code location to a minimal XML spec context bundle in one query","reasoning":"Owner clarification 2026-10-30: when an agent reaches code it does not understand, it must use the same graph/query tool to find the spec related to that code instantly; one search returns only relevant blocks, not the irrelevant corpus. Scope for THIS row: a read-only Auger context query keyed by task ID, XML block ID/ch:trace spec reference, code path, or symbol; deterministic relationship expansion; include task scope and exclusion summary; report active/inactive state and verification. Exclusions: no full-corpus fallback, no code/spec edits, no arbitrary remote URL fetch, no second semantic/LLM backend, no GitReins hook wiring (GR-154). Source: docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#selection-and-assembly, #relationship-and-verification-graph, and #acceptance-criteria (AC-3,AC-4,AC-8,AC-9,AC-14).\nch:trace row=AUG-122 spec=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#selection-and-assembly wave=none:task-not-dispatched test=none:not-implemented doc=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md prompt=none:not-dispatched evidence=none:not-run witness=none:proposal-only verdict=none:not-judged commit=none:not-implemented memory=/project/auger/prd/xml-spec-graph-2026-10-29","acceptance_criteria":"1. Given an Auger task ID, when the context query runs once, then it returns that task block, only its in-scope requirements/acceptance/verification blocks, and a compact explicit out-of-scope list with exclusion reasons; proof: tests/test_spec_context.py::test_task_context_excludes_unrelated_blocks.\n2. Given a source path or symbol with a ch:trace spec reference, when the context query runs, then it resolves the exact XML block and declared graph closure with source file, ID, version, active status, applicability, verification method, and relationship edge; proof: tests/test_spec_context.py::test_code_trace_context.\n3. Given no trace, an unknown symbol, an inactive block, or an ambiguous match, when the context query runs, then it returns an explicit structured unscoped/ambiguous/inactive result and never substitutes a whole-document or whole-corpus dump; proof: dedicated negative fixtures.\n4. Given the same query and XML tree, when run twice, then selected IDs, provenance order, and serialized output are byte-identical; proof: golden JSON fixture plus repeated digest equality.\n5. Given a corpus containing unrelated active blocks, when a narrow task/code query runs, then none of those unrelated blocks appear in the response and the response reports selected count, dependency count, input bytes, and output bytes; proof: decoy-block fixture and benchmark JSON.\n6. Out of scope: this query does not dispatch work, write boards, edit code, or call an LLM; proof: tests use a read-only fixture and assert no write/client seams are invoked.","depends_on":["AUG-118","AUG-121"],"files_changed":[],"foreman_note":"PARTIAL - DO NOT REBUILD THE HALF THAT WORKS (measured 2026-11-05, HEAD 10ef0d7). EXISTS (landed ea819d9): one-query resolution of a block by ID or selector plus its declared graph closure, with provenance. Proven live: 'spec list --id AUG-SHARED-DETERMINISM' -> shared.xml#AUG-SHARED-DETERMINISM (a block resolved out of a second file), and 'spec assemble' returns matched + closure blocks with source, version and status fields. MISSING: the task-scoped minimal context bundle - no in-scope/out-of-scope split with exclusion reasons, no ch:trace path/symbol resolution, and the AC's named proof file tests/test_spec_context.py does not exist. Build the task-context layer over the working selection primitive; the primitive itself is done and tested (tests/test_xml_specs.py::test_selects_only_requested_blocks_and_their_dependencies, ::test_no_deps_emits_only_the_matched_block, ::test_verifies_expands_from_the_requirement_not_from_the_criterion).\n\nSG7 dispatch 2026-11-06 (goal auger-xml-hardening). Writer laun